# msil-prog.py --shlibs (plan 5.12.3, 5.12.4; M22), from what it prints when
# %msil_prog_build runs with the stand-ins of lit.local.cfg (prog-cc.py
# records the inputs of every link in <output>.inputs; a later --shlibs wins
# over the empty one of %msil_prog_build). The specification is the cyclic
# pair '?b=b.c;a=a.c,a2.c;b=b.c':
# (1) MSIL mode (obj): the libraries come first, in the order of the
#     specification: b's interface (b.c compiled into shlib-iface-obj/b/,
#     linked with -shared and -Wl,--interface-only into shlib-iface/b.dll),
#     library a (two sources into shlib-obj/a/, linked against b's
#     interface), library b (linked against a); each library link is the
#     program link's prefix (clang, --ld-path=, -<L>, %{msil_ldflags}) with
#     -shared, never the --lib or --native-lib arguments; then the program's
#     sources and archive, and its link names shlib/a.dll and shlib/b.dll
#     after the archive and before the --lib and --native-lib arguments.
#     The records show the earlier library on each link (b's interface on
#     a's), and the program runs with the libraries beside it (msil-run.py
#     --dep-dir; the stand-in program calls each library at run time) and
#     fails without them;
# (2) the same under lto: -flto compiles everywhere;
# (3) native mode, windows-msvc (a Windows host, where the stand-in's
#     native programs are .NET Framework executables): every compile adds
#     -fms-runtime-lib=dll (one C runtime), b's interface is the -shared link
#     with -Wl,/force:unresolved, of which only shlib-iface/b.lib is kept,
#     the libraries link against the import libraries with
#     %{msil_native_ldflags} last, and the program links shlib/a.lib and
#     shlib/b.lib after its archive; it runs with shlib/ beside it;
# (4) native mode, E7: every compile is -fPIC (start.c keeps E7's flags), no
#     interface is built, 'ld.lld -shared -Bsymbolic --as-needed -soname
#     lib<name>.so -rpath $ORIGIN' links each library against the earlier
#     ones and the sysroot's libraries (each library finds the libraries it
#     needs next to it), and the program link (-rpath $ORIGIN) names
#     shlib/liba.so and shlib/libb.so after its archive;
# (5) native mode, Linux with the driver recipe: -fPIC compiles, no
#     interface, -shared links with -Wl,-Bsymbolic, -Wl,-soname,lib<name>.so,
#     -Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN and %{msil_native_ldflags}, and -Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN on
#     the program link too;
# (6) --det builds the libraries in both builds and compares them, their
#     objects and the interface too: a library that records the build
#     directory differs, and only it;
# (7) without --shlibs every build directory has an empty shlib/, which the
#     composites pass as --dep-dir, and no library command runs;
# (8) usage errors (status 2): a malformed specification, a bad name, a
#     library or an interface named twice, an interface after its library
#     or without one, an empty source, and --shlibs with --link-output il;
# (9) --equiv-skip with a 'skip O4' line for the test (plan 5.12.6, M22's
#     lines for msil/test/M2/04-shared/ and the p2c-* rows) builds neither
#     the equivalence link nor the --also-il text of a build with --shlibs,
#     whose link has no --lto-emit-asm text.

